<Adjustable Pomodoro Timer>

Hackster page includes build and user instructions
https://www.hackster.io/paige-rennie/edes-301-pomodoro-timer-723d7a

It has been proven that if you study or do homework for shorter amounts of time with small breaks instead of trying to power through for hours in a row, you end up being able to concentrate for longer in the long term!

I can use my phone or laptop to do this, but not having it displayed in front of me isn’t helpful. Also, sometimes I just need my phone to be away from me (out of sight, out of mind!) so having it on a device that isn’t attached to my phone would be helpful! So that's how I decided to make this Pomodoro Study timer in physical form inspired by the actual website version called Pomofocus.

project_01.py is the main code that controls the LEDs, buzzer and display based on user input from the potentiometer and buttons. 

This project imports code from button.py, buzzer.py, potentiometer.py, led.py, ht16k33.py to run the main code.

Additionally, there is a run script that imports these codes scripts. The configure_pins.sh sets the pins to be pwm, i2c or pwm.

! ! ! 
To run this code, use sudo ./run and this will run the 'run' code which includes project_01.py and configure_pins.sh.
